The concentration of sodium fluoride is 0.044% (w/v). This means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride are dissolved in 100 mL of the solution.

Given a 10 mL dose, we can use the formula:
\[
\text{mass of NaF} = \text{concentration} \times \text{volume}
\]
\[
\text{mass of NaF} = 0.044 \text{ g/100 mL} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
\]
Since the question asks for the mass in milligrams, we need to convert grams to milligrams.
1 g = 1000 mg, so:
\[
0.0044 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
\]

Thus, a 10 mL dose of PhlOR-flex Daily Therapy soap contains 4.4 mg of sodium fluoride.

