The concentration of the photosensitizer should be optimized to ensure an efficient photochemical reaction. If the concentration is too low, the rate of the reaction may be limited by the number of photosensitizer molecules present. If the concentration is too high, the presence of the photosensitizer may cause fluorescence or other effects that reduce the efficiency of the reaction.

5. Definition of the duration of exposure:

The duration of exposure is the time for which the reaction mixture is exposed to light.

