The general process of photosensation involves the following steps:

a. Absorption of light by the photosensitizer molecule (I) to form an excited state (I*):
I + hv → I*

b. Energy transfer from the excited photosensitizer (I*) to the reactants (R) to form reactive intermediates (R*):
I* + R → I + R*

c. Reaction of the reactive intermediate (R+) to form the product (P):
R+ → P

