   - The perimeter \( P \) of ""П"" is calculated as follows:
     \[
     P = \text{Sum of all side lengths visible on the shape}
     \]
   - Horizontal components: \( (4x + 2x) + 2x = 8x \)
   - Vertical components: \( 4 \times 4x = 16x \)
   - Total perimeter combines both horizontal and vertical parts:
     \[ \text{Perimeter} = 2 \times (length + width) = 56 \text{ (given)}
     \]

