","The arithmetic set is given by the form:
\[ a_n = a_1 + (n - 1)d \]
where \( a_1 = 19 \) and \( d \) is the common difference.
The second term is \( a_2 = 19 + 1 \cdot d = 19 + d \).
The third term is \( a_3 = 19 + 2 \cdot d = 19 + 2d \).
The fourth term is \( a_4 = 19 + 3 \cdot d = 19 + 3d \).
The fifth term is \( a_5 = 19 + 4 \cdot d = 19 + 4d \).
The sixth term is \( a_6 = 19 + 5 \cdot d = 19 + 5d \).

Given that the terms become negative from the sixth term, this means that \( a_6 > 0 \) and \( a_7 < 0 \).
Thus, \( a_6 = 19 + 5d > 0 \) and \( a_7 = 19 + 6d < 0 \).

From \( 19 + 5d < 0 \), we have \( 5d < -19 \), so \( d < \frac{-19}{5} = -3.8 \).
From \( 19 + 6d > 0 \), we have \( 6d < -19 \), so \( d > \frac{-19}{6} = -3.166 \ldots \).

