","(a) The force on the proton is \(F = qE\), where \(q = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C}\) and \(E = 500 \, \text{N/C}\). The force is:
\[ F = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C})(500 \, \text{N/C}) = 8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N} \]
Using Newton's second law, \(F = ma\), we can find the acceleration:
\[ a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} \approx 4.79 \times 10^{9} \, \text{m/s}^2 \]

(b) The probe starts from rest, so \(v_0 = 0\). Using the kinematic formula \(v = v_0 + at\), we can find the time it takes to reach \(v = 35,000 \, \text{m/s}\):
\[ 35,000 = 0 + (4.79 \times 10^9 \, \text{m/s}^2) t \]
Solving for \(t\):
\[ t = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s}}{4.79 \times 10^9 \, \text{m/s}^2} \approx 7.32 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{s} \]

