   The molar mass of \( \text{NO}_2 \) is \( 14 + 2 \times 16 = 14 + 32 = 46 \text{ g/mol} \).  
   The equilibrium is:  
   \[
   \text{N}_2\text{O}_4 \rightleftharpoons 2\text{NO}_2
   \]  
   Let \( \alpha \) be the equilibrium constant.  
   At equilibrium, the moles of \( \text{NO}_2 \) are \( 2\alpha \) and \( 1 - \alpha \) moles of \( \text{N}_2\text{O}_4 \).  
